# Gitignored files to copy into every new worktree (--worktree, EnterWorktree,
# subagent-driven-development). Syntax is .gitignore-style: only files that
# are BOTH listed here AND gitignored get copied — tracked files never do.
#
# Kept intentionally minimal. A worktree should be a disposable checkout:
# copy only what's needed to make `just check` / `just audit` / `just test` /
# `just run-server` behave the same as in the main checkout. Everything else
# (venv, caches, models, the brain DB, logs, enrollment photos) is either
# regenerable per-worktree or must NOT be duplicated across parallel agents.

# Runtime config — without this the app can't start (settings.py reads .env)
.env
.env.local

# Baselines compared against by pre-commit / just audit — without these,
# every worktree treats all existing findings as "new"
.secrets.baseline
.bandit-baseline
